jerina is a well-funded, high-profile challenger with national GOP backing"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a modest Democratic edge: incumbency and money favor Cuellar in a district with a slight Republican lean, and the lone recent poll shows him up 11. Markets and most raters agree on a Likely-to-Lean D outcome, so a margin near 7-8 points fits the evidence without overreacting to thin polling.", "watch": "A late surge from Tijerina's national-profile campaign or further erosion of Cuellar's standing with South Texas Latino voters could tighten the race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Henry Cuellar (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Henry Cuellar seeks another term in a South Texas district that leans slightly Republican but that he has held for years through shifting political tides. His Republican challenger, Webb County Judge Tano Tijerina, has run a visible, well-funded campaign with national conservative attention, including appearances on Fox and Newsmax and a meeting with former Education Secretary Linda McMahon. Cuellar has raised more than $2.2 million and holds a cash advantage, and a new redistricting map may have modestly improved his position.\n\nThe evidence points to a Cuellar win with a mid-single-digit margin. An August poll showed him ahead by 11 points, prediction markets put his chances near 90 percent, and expert ratings mostly land at Lean D or Likely D, though one rates it Tilt D. His lukewarm endorsement from LUPE Votes and corruption attacks from Tijerina are risks, but nothing yet suggests the race has moved into tossup territory.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9009, "margin": 7.69}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8765, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8779, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8804, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8627, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8617, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8973,